<title>USA: TABLE - Browning-Ferris Q3 oper shr rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Browning-Ferris Q3 oper shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Period ended June 30.</p>
<p>				1997			1996</p>
<p> Oper shr		   $0.45		    $0.31</p>
<p> Oper net		  90,717		   62,022</p>
<p> Revs		   1,471,252		1,471,368</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 204,020		  200,932</p>
<p>	  9  MONTHS</p>
<p> Oper shr		   $1.14		    $0.97</p>
<p> Oper net		 230,428		  193,857</p>
<p> Revs		   4,380,120		4,276,036</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 203,019		  200,395</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: First Call Q3 consensus oper shr: $0.43.</p>
<p>1997 Q3 and nine month periods exclude pretax charges of $84.1 million, or $0.25 a share. The charge was taken to reduce staff, divest underperforming assets, and cut operating costs.</p>
